{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00557 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxyzine, an antihistamine, is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis through a series of indications that collectively suggest a potential mechanism of action. The evidence shows that Hydroxyzine is associated with Allergic Rhinitis, which in turn is linked to several drugs, including Ramatroban and Mebhydrolin, all of which are indicated for Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests that Hydroxyzine may exert a therapeutic effect on Vasomotor Rhinitis through a shared pathway involving allergic inflammation. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications for Vasomotor Rhinitis implies that the condition may be influenced by a common mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of inflammatory pathways or the suppression of allergic responses. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Hydroxyzine to be repurposed for Vasomotor Rhinitis, based on its established role in managing allergic rhinitis.",
